From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nikolajs Agafonovs <nikolajs.agafonovs@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 13:06:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] html: inline-flex boxes placed on their line

The last pass of line layout positioned replaced inlines and inline
blocks but left inline-flex boxes out: they kept their unplaced x and y
and the line was not made as tall as them (0px for a line holding only
one).  YouTube's logo fell out of the masthead.
---
 netsurf/content/handlers/html/layout.c | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/netsurf/content/handlers/html/layout.c b/netsurf/content/handlers/html/layout.c
index 09d3db1..f3ae4db 100644
--- a/netsurf/content/handlers/html/layout.c
+++ b/netsurf/content/handlers/html/layout.c
@@ -3405,8 +3405,11 @@ layout_line(struct box *first,
 				used_height = d->height;
 			}
 		} else if ((d->type == BOX_INLINE) ||
-				d->type == BOX_INLINE_BLOCK) {
-			/* replaced inlines and inline-blocks */
+				d->type == BOX_INLINE_BLOCK ||
+				d->type == BOX_INLINE_FLEX) {
+			/* replaced inlines, inline-blocks and inline-flexes
+			 * (inline-flexes were left out: not placed on the
+			 * line, and the line not as tall as them) */
 			d->x += x0;
 			d->y = *y + d->border[TOP].width + d->margin[TOP];
 			h = d->margin[TOP] + d->border[TOP].width +
